# ECS Builder Pattern

## Creating Entities

Always use the Builder pattern for creating entities:

```typescript
const player = new ECS.Builder(scene)
  .withName('player')
  .asSprite(texture)
  .localPos(100, 200)
  .scale(2, 2)
  .anchor(0.5, 0.5)
  .withTag('player')
  .withFlag(PlayerFlags.ALIVE)
  .withState(PlayerStates.IDLE)
  .withAttribute('health', 100)
  .withComponent(new PlayerController())
  .build();
```

## Builder Method Categories

### Object Type (choose one)
- `asContainer()` - Empty container
- `asSprite(texture)` - Sprite
- `asText(text, style)` - Text
- `asGraphics()` - Graphics
- etc.

### Position & Transform
- `localPos(x, y)` - Position relative to parent
- `globalPos(x, y)` - World position
- `scale(x, y?)` - Scale
- `anchor(x, y)` - Anchor point
- `rotation(angle)` - Rotation

### Metadata
- `withName(name)` - Name for searching
- `withTag(tag)` - Tag for grouping
- `withFlag(flag)` - Bit flag
- `withState(state)` - State ID

### Behavior
- `withComponent(component)` - Add component
- `withAttribute(key, value)` - Add attribute

### Hierarchy
- `withParent(parent)` - Set parent
- `withChild(builder)` - Add child

## Factory Functions

Extract entity creation into reusable functions:

```typescript
export function createPlayer(scene: ECS.Scene, x: number, y: number) {
  return new ECS.Builder(scene)
    .withName('player')
    .asSprite(PIXI.Texture.from('player'))
    .localPos(x, y)
    .withTag('player')
    .withComponent(new PlayerController())
    .build();
}
```

## Global Components (Systems)

Add systems as global components:

```typescript
scene.addGlobalComponent(new CollisionSystem());
scene.addGlobalComponent(new KeyInputComponent());
```
